This doc file applies to Version 1.3 - Note there are a lot of new functions
and changes to this version, as well as bug fixes extreme. Please look at the
changes.doc file for more information.


Description:  Zwall - the Best Graffiti wall ever.

Installation: Put the whole ZWall directory in in your Doors: assign.

The script is called from your Doors menu like this:

Option_W:
  CallScript 'Doors:Zwall/Zwall
  Signal MenuLoop

Or add it somewhere in your PostLogon.zeus with the line:

  CallScript 'Doors:Zwall/Zwall'



Usage:

Come on.. :) Use cursor up and down keys to scroll through the
entries. S to spray your own one.. Press P to edit the
Preferences (applies to you and the users) where you can knock
up your own little signature to sign your entry on the wall, and
choose your own colours for each line etc....

The extra Sysop options panel appears dependent on your access
level and gives you extra options such as Delete the current
displayed message, and also reset the wall totally. Both of
these options can be configured via the Config file so that
nobody who shouldn't have access to them, can use them, even
though they will not be displayed anyway..

Also you can have deleted messages displayed in the logfile so
you can view a deleted message yourself to see what the
deleter found so offensive :) That too is optional within the
config file.

Also allowing the user to press Return to exit Zwall is optional
within the Configuration file. Q works regardless, but this is a kind
of slow down the anoying user who hammers his return key to get past
your BBS intro screens and get to the File menu :-(

Press T or B to go to Top or Bottom of the Wall.

The Sysop keys are: D to delete current message, and R to reset the wall.

Note: The salvage operation is working now but all it does at this time is
      purge the wall data and reinitialise everything if essential files are
      missing. You can specify in the config if you wish this automated or 
      not.

Configuration:

There is a seperate config file which is remarked within for adjusting
all kinds of access levels for Delete entry access, reset wall etc etc.. 

LogFile:

Zwall maintains its own log file which keeps track of users
Entering messages (optional in the config file) and also logs
important errors.. IE: the user will be prompted to notify you
if there is an error in the Zwall program execution, but the
Logfile will specify the exact error within. This is forced, so
you may disable the logging of normal usage in the config file
if you don't want it getting too heavy :-)

Future Support:

Dependant on feedback idealy. I've spent a long time writing
this little program, hopefully as a support program to go with
the full release of Zeus BBS as part of the default set up
etc.. I'd like to improve upon it some more but I need ideas
etc which I'm not sure how much I'll get at the moment with
Zeus not released as yet etc. See seperate doc file todo.doc for a few
general ideas I've had should I work any more on this thing.

